WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.120
Pardon me.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.860
Here is the report on this 
year's tax collection.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.030
I've entrusted that matter entirely to Kurt.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.510
Understood.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.450
Father!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.370
Oh, how are you doing, Karl?

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.340
Darling, you have a visitor at the mansion.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.460
Oh? That's rare here in the countryside.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.170
Um...

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.300
They said they wished to 
speak to you about Wendelin.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.180
This is from Head Auditor 
Ruckner in the capital.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.180
Lord Commissioner Ruckner's 
younger brother, then?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:50.650
I bet it's just another request to join 
the family that Wendelin is part of, right?

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:54.220
Listen, I don't care how famous 
that boy becomes in the capital.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.080
It has nothing to do with us out here!

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.920
I wish these trifling requests would 
stop coming to me, the family heir.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.080
Oh, no!

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.290
What's the matter, Amalie?

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.250
This says that Wendelin has passed 
away while exploring ancient ruins.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.550
<i>After three years of harsh 
training with that magician,</i>

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.160
<i>I'm finally an adult.</i>

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.660
<i>At last, I can make my debut as an adventurer!</i>

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.600
<i>Do I look good, Master?</i>

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.540
Registering as adventurers 
sure was easy, huh?

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.370
The people at the guild were all business.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.160
But according to this,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.980
we'll be hunting in the local 
area for a while at first,

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.870
so it's not worth celebrating much.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.830
Adventurer's
Manual

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.420
You seem happy, Wendelin.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.800
Our days as adventurers 
are just getting started!

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.260
Up until now, I've been hogtied
 by the obligations of nobility,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.370
but starting today, 
things will be different!

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.720
No one can steal my freedom anymore!

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.500
Sorry to interrupt the celebration.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.810
Brantag?

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:13.220
Your new party has received a request 
to explore some ancient ruins.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.650
Ancient ruins?

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.610
Mandatory Quest From the King

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.610
To the Dragon Busters

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.610
we hereby order you to undertake the following quest

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.610
A mandatory quest from the king?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.570
You can't turn it down, of course.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.580
<i>Huh? Nothing has changed at all.</i>

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:54.150
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:01.970
Um, our new party advisor is supposed 
to be an active adventurer, right?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.840
Episode 8
Presumed Dead? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.260
But you're...

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.130
My lord's ordered my 
temporary return to action.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:13.440
Well, we couldn't ask for a better advisor.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:19.000
My lord doesn't want you all to die, after all.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.150
Are these ruins that dangerous?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.640
Three years ago, was it?

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.630
These ruins were discovered 
after we defeated Greigorland.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.640
There was an entrance to 
something underground,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.040
and the adventurer's guild 
sent several people into it.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.520
But they never came back?

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.340
Exactly.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:45.970
So then the guild sent some experienced 
adventurers to follow up...

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.180
But they never came back.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.170
That's when the guild realized

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:00.070
that if these underground ruins 
could take down such veterans...

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.810
Then there's probably a dragon?

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.050
Correct.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.480
And that's why you were given this quest.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.280
What about that makes it a valid reason?

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:14.750
Think about it. What did you guys call 
yourselves when you registered?

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.930
The Dragon Busters.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.710
Get it now?

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.630
There's nothing here.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.670
Anyway, is a party supposed to act like this?

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:33.110
We can't help it!

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.870
If a dragon breathes on us out of nowhere,

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.900
we'll all be reduced to ash in an instant!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.740
We'll be burned to ash on our first quest!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:42.570
Please be our shield, Sir Magic Barrier!

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.550
Doesn't look like you have to worry 
about turning to ash, at least.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:52.210
I cast my detection spell, but I'm not 
even sensing any weak enemies.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.500
Over there! A door!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.580
Let's go.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.810
All right, nothing here, either.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.420
Doesn't that seem odd, though?

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.730
Where are the adventurers 
who never returned?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:22.690
It can't be...

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.010
Get out of this room at once! Hurry!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.490
Huh? What is this?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.950
My feet are stuck to the floor! I can't move!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.990
Tsk! It's a trap left by the 
ancient magic civilization.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.750
Listen up, everyone! Be prepared 
for battle at any moment!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.770
Even I don't know what's going to—

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.170
Brantag!

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:52.780
No way...

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.620
Wendelin!

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:55.560
Elise!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.000
W-Wendelin...

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.330
Welcome to Reverse Hanging

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.830
"Welcome to Reverse Hanging"...

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.310
What is this?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.450
That was a trap from the 
ancient magic civilization.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:29.660
It uses magic circles to teleport 
victims down to the bottom floor,

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.440
forcing them to make their way back to 
the surface if they want to survive.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.360
I'd only ever read about it, myself.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.640
Reach the surface from the bottom floor?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.560
That's easy, right, Well?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.060
Huh?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.920
Show us that te-le-port-ing!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.400
Tell them.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.430
Uh, in order to use teleportation,

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.640
I need complete awareness 
of where I'm teleporting to,

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.120
as well as where I currently am.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.990
But I don't know where we are right now, so...

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.090
Oh, Elise, you're awake.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.170
Are you all right?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.780
I'm sorry for worrying you.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:09.110
Now we're all safely together.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.170
That's a good thing,

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.540
but you're telling us you 
can't use teleportation here?!

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.080
Then what are we supposed to do?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.040
We climb up normally?

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.300
Whoever built these ruins...

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.640
...was an awful person.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.410
So, I wonder what's lying 
in wait for us here.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.230
Let's go.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.870
Whoever built these ruins...

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:10.940
...was deranged.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.780
Nowhere to run, huh?

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.520
Tsk! Looks like they're waking up, too.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.720
Everyone, step back! I'll use magic to—

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.930
You should be the one to step back, Well.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:30.050
We have no idea how many more 
floors we'll have to climb up,

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:33.260
so you should hold off on any major 
spells and conserve your magic.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.590
As long as it's not dragon's breath,
 we can hold our own.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.550
All of you...

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.510
It's finally time to show off 
the fruits of my training!

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:56.850
Wow...

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.660
A wall of wind?

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:06.120
Boy! You and I should support them by using 
wind magic to limit the golems' movement,

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.760
and keep them from surrounding 
the three on the front lines!

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.970
Roger that!

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:15.460
Young Elise, you stay back in the rear 
and focus on healing their injuries!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.670
Understood.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:22.640
All of you, remember to avoid wasting stamina 
and magic needed for the long battles to come!

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.450
Now, let's get through this!

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:25.600
Right!

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.090
Their formation crumbled after we 
defeated the mounted golem leading them!

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.040
Now's our chance!

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:37.030
Okay!

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.120
It's my first time using this in actual battle,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:42.300
but I can test it out plenty here!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.500
Here's the result of my 
training with that magician!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.110
Magic Shock Wave!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.960
It's over.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.420
Everyone okay?

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:58.890
Somehow.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.320
I'm fine, too—

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.940
What is it? Bugs?

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:06.310
That's...

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.270
The adventurers who failed 
to explore this place, huh?

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.730
Quiet!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.020
There are Golems above us!

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.460
They're not giving us any time to rest.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.530
Hurry!

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:27.160
Let's go!

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.920
How long is this going to go on?

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:34.900
Who knows?

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.040
It's been five days.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:49.070
The irresponsible birds around the 
palace are saying they're dead.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.870
If Baron Baumeister were to perish there...

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:59.490
It would serve those who 
supported the Baron right.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.940
Cardinal Hohenheim,

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:08.010
I heard the news about your 
granddaughter and her fiancé.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.950
You must be beside yourself with worry.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.860
Not at all.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.940
I'm certain they shall return alive.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:15.820
Farewell.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.300
Cardinal Hohenheim.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:27.380
Oh, Lord Commissioner Ruckner.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.900
They're dead?

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.410
Who's spreading such a rumor?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:39.270
I imagine you must be fraught 
with worry yourself.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.240
The day you become Lord 
Commissioner is nigh, my lord.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.040
Listen. Next, you shall head to 
the remote land in the south

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.410
and meet with the eldest brother, Kurt.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:56.960
Then I want you to encourage him to have 
his sons succeed Baron Baumeister.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.440
As you wish.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:03.840
You'd better be dead, Baron Baumeister.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.220
Your food's so good, Elise!

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.610
Did you get enough sleep?

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.170
Yes, about two hours just now.

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:22.690
Taking shifts eating and sleeping to recover 
our stamina in response to these long battles...

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.460
It's a good strategy, but...

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:32.270
Sorry for making you use your magic.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:33.460
Nonsense.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.580
When would I use it,
 if not at times like this?

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:38.540
We can't keep this up forever.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:43.510
Now, Wendelin, you need to rest—

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:57.770
It's because of that magician's training 
that we're able to do this now, too.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:21.460
Damn! How long is this going to go on?

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.740
I hope the next one's...

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.850
Magic Shock Wave!

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:47.280
We might just die at this rate.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:52.240
Don't worry. That's not going to happen.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:55.700
I suppose I can't die yet.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:00.690
I haven't won a single match 
against Warren yet.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.970
If I died now, I'd regret it.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:09.780
Regret...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.500
Wendelin...

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.990
Let's make sure we get home alive.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.410
Otherwise, I'll regret it.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.870
Right.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.360
None here.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.960
We did it!

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.890
It's over!

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.200
It's over now?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.990
Get back!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.280
This one's a dragon golem!

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:21.980
Right when we don't have much magic left!

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.300
Iina!

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.180
Iina, please hang in there!

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:01.340
Don't worry. I promise I'll save Iina!

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:08.420
Things are just going to get worse if 
we keep maintaining this magic barrier.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:12.670
How are you doing?

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.410
Thanks. I'm fine now.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:18.340
Your healing magic really is a lifesaver.

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:24.010
Then we'll crush that dragon golem.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.740
But that thing's body is 
probably made of mythril.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.890
Most magic spells won't even scratch—

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:33.690
If we concentrate all of our remaining 
magic as much as possible...

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:37.300
I see. It's worth trying.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.810
I'll bet all of my magic power on you.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:46.540
Here we go!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.920
Brantag!

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.760
You really are just like him, you know.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:10.700
Brantag...

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:19.590
Yes! Try harder, Well!

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:25.250
You shouldn't tell someone 
who's trying hard to try harder!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.210
Well's magic power is all...

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:38.980
Sorry, everyone... I...

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:41.230
Well...

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:45.560
Elise?

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.120
This is...

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:53.980
This is a spell called Miracle's Light!

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:58.360
A kiss?!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.060
Huh? It stopped?

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:52.920
Well!

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:03.760
That healing spell she 
just used, Miracle's Light...

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.740
Fundamentally, it's a spell 
to recover one's stamina,

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.800
but I've heard it can recover 
some degree of magical power, too.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:15.170
So do you have to kiss the person to use it?

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:16.420
No way.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.650
The church wouldn't allow that, either.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.110
So you're saying she took advantage 
of the chaos to kiss him?!

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:25.300
Well, we very well might have died there,

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:29.130
so I imagine she felt she'd regret it 
if she didn't kiss the man she loves.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.650
Hey, this is incredible!

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.290
Come here and have a look!

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:36.410
Come on, we're totally exhausted right now.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.710
If this isn't <i>really</i> incredible,

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:42.660
I'll use what strength I have 
left to beat you black and blue!

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.660
Hurry up!

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.760
Yes, yes, we're coming.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.120
Why are you so excited?

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.660
Just come over here!

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.180
This had better be incredible!

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.420
It is!

00:20:57.490 --> 00:21:00.530
Apparently, the mage from 
the ancient magic civilization

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:05.570
who created that nasty underground 
ruin was Count Ichelberg.

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:08.510
He was a leading creator of magic items.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:12.040
But why would he create 
something that elaborate?

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.710
He probably wanted to test people's talent,

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.500
to see if they would be worth 
entrusting a legacy like that to.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:20.910
Legacy?

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:24.380
Well, come look at this! It's incredible!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.310
Look at that!

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.770
They're the ancient airships that 
form the core of our magic airships.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:35.050
Wow...

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:40.210
Brantag was saying that no one 
has ever discovered so many at once!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.580
That's not all, either.
